Congressman Ken Calvert (CA-41) sent a letter to the Riverside County Board of Supervisors raising concerns about inherently biased ads placed by the Riverside County Registrar of Voters that encouraged voting among very select populations prior to the November general election. Recent reporting discovered the Riverside County Registrar of Voters placed ads on Meta platforms using targeting keywords that included “Gangsta rap,” “Wiz Khalifa,” “Rick Ross,” “Kanye West,” and “2 Chainz” among others. A portion of the ads were also targeted to one specific zip code, located in downtown Riverside. “Americans expect those who conduct our elections to do so in a manner that is fair and without any political bias,” said Rep. Calvert. “The decision by the Riverside County Registrar of Voters office to spend tax dollars to encourage select populations of voters to cast a ballot in the November election is deeply troubling. Riverside County voters deserve to know why the Registrar of Voters wants fans of ‘gangsta rap’ to vote more than fans of other genres, like country music. Riverside County voters also deserve to know why the Registrar of Voters wants residents of a single downtown Riverside zip code to vote more than residents in other zip codes.” According to the Meta Ad Library database, the Riverside County Registrar of Voters targeted ads using the following keywords: Erykah Badu, Freestyle rap, Future (rapper), Gangsta rap, Gucci Mane, Janelle Monáe, Jay-Z, Jhené Aiko, Jill Scott, Kanye West, Kehlani, Meek Mill, Metro Boomin, Migos, Rae Sremmurd, Rapping, Rick Ross, Solange Knowles, Soul music, Southern hip hop, SZA (singer), T.I., Teyana Taylor, Tinashe, Tory Lanez, Underground hip hop, Wiz Khalifa. Meta’s disclosure database also indicates that more than 10 percent of social media ads placed by the Riverside County ROV were geographically targeted to a single zip code, 92501, located in downtown Riverside. In 2024, a Cornell University study found that hip-hop and rap music streaming online occurs more heavily in Democratic-leaning communities than in Republican-leaning region. Furthermore, according to a YouGov poll conducted in 2024, Democrats are twice as likely as Republicans to name hip-hop as their favorite genre. ### Office Locations Washington DC Office 2205 Rayburn Building Washington, DC 20515 Phone: (202) 225-1986 Fax: (202) 225-2004 Palm Desert Office 73585 Fred Waring Drive Suite 108 Palm Desert, CA 92260 Phone: (760) 620-0041 Corona Office 400 S. Vicentia Avenue Suite 125 Corona, CA 92882 Phone: (951) 277-0042 Fax: (951) 277-0420 const allHomepageWebforms = document.querySelectorAll('#webform-submission-webform-225-node-43-add-form'); if (allHomepageWebforms[0] !== null) { allHomepageWebforms.forEach(form => { form.insertAdjacentHTML('beforebegin', ` `); }) } body > #evo-displayer-background-dim { display: none !important; } Copyright Privacy House.gov Accessibility RSS body[class*="path-"] { background: #fff url(/sites/evo-subsites/calvert.house.gov/files/evo-media-image/homepage-background.jpg) fixed top no-repeat!important; } iframe { border: none; border: 0 } table[aria-label="Recent Votes Table"] thead th { color: #fff; } const evoHomeButton = document.querySelector('#superfish-main'); if (evoHomeButton !== null) { evoHomeButton.insertAdjacentHTML('afterbegin', ` `); } {"path":{"baseUrl":"/","pathPrefix":"","currentPath":"node/4741","currentPathIsAdmin":false,"isFront":false,"currentLanguage":"en"},"pluralDelimiter":"","suppressDeprecationErrors":true,"gtag":{"tagId":"","consentMode":false,"otherIds":[],"events":[],"additionalConfigInfo":[]},"gtm":{"tagId":null,"settings":{"data_layer":"dataLayer","include_environment":false},"tagIds":["GTM-TQX94K2"]},"data":{"extlink":{"extTarget":true,"extTargetAppendNewWindowDisplay":true,"extTargetAppendNewWindowLabel":"(opens in a new window)","extTargetNoOverride":true,"extNofollow":true,"extTitleNoOverride":false,"extNoreferrer":true,"extFollowNoOverride":true,"extCl