Today, Congressman Ken Calvert (CA-41) announced and congratulated the 2026 Service Academy Appointees from the 41st Congressional District. “I want to congratulate the outstanding students who have been appointed to attend our service academies,” said Rep. Calvert. “Nominating extraordinary students from our region to attend the academies is one of the highest honors I’m afforded as a U.S. Representative. In addition to the students, I want to thank their families, friends, teachers, and everyone who supported them. Our volunteer military is shaped by selfless citizens who step forward to serve, and I’m humbled by the inspiring leadership and achievements these students demonstrate at such a young age. Their dedication brings honor to our community, and I am proud to recognize each of their successes.” The following candidates were nominated by Rep. Calvert through a highly competitive process conducted by the Congressional Nominations Selection Committee. After review by the respective academies, each student received and accepted an Offer of Appointment during the 2026 admissions cycle. They will join the Class of 2030, entering in June 2026. U.S. Air Force Academy: Ian Cho, Eastvale – Eleanor Roosevelt High School Ethan Miller, La Quinta - La Quinta High School Matthew Woodroof, Lake Elsinore, Murrieta Valley High School (Class of 2025) - attended the US Air Force Preparatory School. U.S. Naval Academy: Kevin Chen, Eastvale – Marine Military Academy Jera Nalu Likins, Menifee – Santa Rosa Academy (Class of 2025) - attended the US Naval Academy Preparatory School. U.S. Military Academy at West Point: Daniel Kambe, La Quinta – Xavier College Preparatory Alexander Krishan, Winchester – Murrieta Mesa High School (Class of 2025) - attended the US Military Academy Preparatory School. U.S. Merchant Marine Academy: Sean Lee, Corona – EF Academy Pasadena Luke Woodroof, Lake Elsinore – Elsinore High School The achievements of these appointees reflect the strength and potential of our community. Their commitment to serve and pursue excellence at our nation's prestigious academies deserves our highest admiration. We celebrate their accomplishments and look forward to the leadership and positive impact they will bring to our country. Let us be inspired by their dedication as we continue to support future generations who strive for excellence and service. Office Locations Washington DC Office 2205 Rayburn Building Washington, DC 20515 Phone: (202) 225-1986 Fax: (202) 225-2004 Palm Desert Office 73585 Fred Waring Drive Suite 108 Palm Desert, CA 92260 Phone: (760) 620-0041 Corona Office 400 S. Vicentia Avenue Suite 125 Corona, CA 92882 Phone: (951) 277-0042 Fax: (951) 277-0420 const allHomepageWebforms = document.querySelectorAll('#webform-submission-webform-225-node-43-add-form'); if (allHomepageWebforms[0] !== null) { allHomepageWebforms.forEach(form => { form.insertAdjacentHTML('beforebegin', ` `); }) } body > #evo-displayer-background-dim { display: none !important; } Copyright Privacy House.gov Accessibility RSS body[class*="path-"] { background: #fff url(/sites/evo-subsites/calvert.house.gov/files/evo-media-image/homepage-background.jpg) fixed top no-repeat!important; } iframe { border: none; border: 0 } table[aria-label="Recent Votes Table"] thead th { color: #fff; } const evoHomeButton = document.querySelector('#superfish-main'); if (evoHomeButton !== null) { evoHomeButton.insertAdjacentHTML('afterbegin', ` `); } {"path":{"baseUrl":"/","pathPrefix":"","currentPath":"node/4711","currentPathIsAdmin":false,"isFront":false,"currentLanguage":"en"},"pluralDelimiter":"","suppressDeprecationErrors":true,"gtag":{"tagId":"","consentMode":false,"otherIds":[],"events":[],"additionalConfigInfo":[]},"gtm":{"tagId":null,"settings":{"data_layer":"dataLayer","include_environment":false},"tagIds":["GTM-TQX94K2"]},"data":{"extlink":{"extTarget":true,"extTargetAppendNewWindowDisplay":true,"extTargetAppendNewWindowLabel":"(opens in a new window)","ext