Congressman Ken Calvert (CA-41) introduced a resolution, H.Res. 142, in honor of the 80 th Anniversary of the Battle of Iwo Jima. The critical battle in the Pacific Theater of World War II, in which nearly 7,000 U.S. Marines were killed, began 80 years ago this month and included the iconic raising of the American flag on Mount Suribachi. Rep. Salud Carbajal (CA-24) is a co-lead and original cosponsor of the resolution. “The Battle of Iwo Jima tested the strength and will of the American military in the Pacific,” said Rep. Calvert. “The bravery, sacrifice, and determination displayed by our Marines on Iwo Jima continues to inspire us 80 years later. It’s only fitting for Congress to remember and honor those who gave everything and fought so heroically on Iwo Jima to shape the future of freedom that we enjoy today.” ### Issues : Defense Office Locations Washington DC Office 2205 Rayburn Building Washington, DC 20515 Phone: (202) 225-1986 Fax: (202) 225-2004 Palm Desert Office 73585 Fred Waring Drive Suite 108 Palm Desert, CA 92260 Phone: (760) 620-0041 Corona Office 400 S. Vicentia Avenue Suite 125 Corona, CA 92882 Phone: (951) 277-0042 Fax: (951) 277-0420 const allHomepageWebforms = document.querySelectorAll('#webform-submission-webform-225-node-43-add-form'); if (allHomepageWebforms[0] !== null) { allHomepageWebforms.forEach(form => { form.insertAdjacentHTML('beforebegin', ` `); }) } body > #evo-displayer-background-dim { display: none !important; } Copyright Privacy House.gov Accessibility RSS body[class*="path-"] { background: #fff url(/sites/evo-subsites/calvert.house.gov/files/evo-media-image/homepage-background.jpg) fixed top no-repeat!important; } iframe { border: none; border: 0 } table[aria-label="Recent Votes Table"] thead th { color: #fff; } const evoHomeButton = document.querySelector('#superfish-main'); if (evoHomeButton !== null) { evoHomeButton.insertAdjacentHTML('afterbegin', ` `); } {"path":{"baseUrl":"/","pathPrefix":"","currentPath":"node/4585","c