Today, Defense Appropriations Subcommittee Chairman Ken Calvert (CA-41) issued the following statement in response to the announcement that for the second straight year, the Marine Corps passed an audit: “I want to congratulate Marine Corps Commandant General Eric Smith and our Marines for being accountable to American taxpayers. The Marine Corps continues to be a rare bright spot when it comes to fiscal accountability in the Department of Defense. This audit not only strengthens the Marine Corps' ability to plan, budget, and execute missions with precision but also reinforces their commitment to readiness and operational effectiveness. As Chairman of the Defense Appropriations Subcommittee, I fully expect the other branches of our military to pass a clean audit in the very near future.” ### Issues : Defense Office Locations Washington DC Office 2205 Rayburn Building Washington, DC 20515 Phone: (202) 225-1986 Fax: (202) 225-2004 Palm Desert Office 73585 Fred Waring Drive Suite 108 Palm Desert, CA 92260 Phone: (760) 620-0041 Corona Office 400 S. Vicentia Avenue Suite 125 Corona, CA 92882 Phone: (951) 277-0042 Fax: (951) 277-0420 const allHomepageWebforms = document.querySelectorAll('#webform-submission-webform-225-node-43-add-form'); if (allHomepageWebforms[0] !== null) { allHomepageWebforms.forEach(form => { form.insertAdjacentHTML('beforebegin', ` `); }) } body > #evo-displayer-background-dim { display: none !important; } Copyright Privacy House.gov Accessibility RSS body[class*="path-"] { background: #fff url(/sites/evo-subsites/calvert.house.gov/files/evo-media-image/homepage-background.jpg) fixed top no-repeat!important; } iframe { border: none; border: 0 } table[aria-label="Recent Votes Table"] thead th { color: #fff; } const evoHomeButton = document.querySelector('#superfish-main'); if (evoHomeButton !== null) { evoHomeButton.insertAdjacentHTML('afterbegin', ` `); } {"path":{"baseUrl":"/","pathPrefix":"","currentPath":"node/4573","currentPathIsAdmin":false,"is